 "details": {
  "title": "Moonglow",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Rod Stewart’s record five steps down, in F (G for the trumpet), concert B3 to C5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 91. The A sections keep Rod’s short phrases: “moonglow” held two beats where he holds it, rests where the guitar answers him. In the instrumental the trumpet plays Arturo Sandoval’s chorus as the Fret Finder guitar has it, the tune with his turns: F, D, F, A♭ climbing into A, A♭, A, C over the D♭9♯5, G, F, D♭ out of the long A. A short line leads in over the intro’s falling ninth chords, and the ending sets the tune’s opening once more and comes to rest on A over the last F6/9.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Will Hudson, Eddie DeLange and Irving Mills (1933)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, in the form and chords of Rod Stewart’s record; the instrumental is Arturo Sandoval’s chorus as the Fret Finder page has it"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "F major concert (G for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, A, A, bridge, A and tag, instrumental, bridge, A and tag, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (mg-guitar.mp3), 3:30"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The same numbers as the Fret Finder page"
   ]
  ]
 }
